  "prompt": "Image 1 is the exact character identity and art reference: Noct four-star form: chibi hooded shadow swordsman, soft pointed black hood, completely black hidden face with only two small pale lavender-violet eyes, dark scarf, dark armour under a long layered black half-robe and torn cloak lined with deep violet, small dark boots, ONE long black crescent moon-blade. Keep him exactly; no redesign.\nImage 2 is a scale-and-root template made from the same character: preserve its cell locations, camera distance, body scale, body root at the horizontal centre and the feet line at about 94% of cell height. Change only the pose. Do not reproduce Image 2 as-is and do not draw any guide, border or separator.\nCreate a 6-frame RUN CYCLE moving RIGHT, 3 columns x 2 rows, read left-to-right then next row. A fast, low, leaning assassin run in 3/4 view facing right. He holds the crescent moon-blade in his right hand, trailing low behind him and pointing back-down, close to his body, the same in every frame. The free arm swings opposite to the forward leg. The LEGS MUST ALTERNATE - this is the most important rule:\nFrame 1: CONTACT - RIGHT foot forward touching the ground in front, LEFT leg stretched behind, body lowest.\nFrame 2: PUSH - RIGHT leg under the body bearing weight, LEFT knee bending as the left foot leaves the ground, body rising.\nFrame 3: PASSING - LEFT knee swinging forward past the RIGHT leg, LEFT foot lifted, body highest.\nFrame 4: CONTACT - LEFT foot forward touching the ground in front, RIGHT leg stretched behind, body lowest (mirror of frame 1).\nFrame 5: PUSH - LEFT leg under the body, RIGHT knee bending as the right foot leaves the ground.\nFrame 6: PASSING - RIGHT knee swinging forward past the LEFT leg, RIGHT foot lifted; then the loop returns to frame 1.\nFrames 1-3 and 4-6 must clearly show DIFFERENT legs in front. The torn cloak and robe tatters stream back to the left and ripple with each stride. Torso stays near the cell centre; no travel across the cell. Same scale and camera in every frame; body bobs only a few pixels with the stride.\nBody and held weapon only: no slash arc, no motion lines, no trail, no dust, no smoke, no aura, no particles, no shadow, no ground. Everything fully inside its own cell with at least 5% magenta margin. Exactly 6 frames, 3 columns x 2 rows of equal square 512x512 cells, total 1536x1024. Background 100% solid flat #FF00FF magenta, no gradient, no text, no labels, no gridlines, no borders. Clean HD smooth painted game art, NOT pixel art.\n\n# Frames 4-6: the top row's poses redrawn one by one with the legs swapped (half-b/prompt-far-N.txt, gpt-6-astra high), because whole-sheet prompts kept repeating the same leg.\n",
